## Robustness (`sensitivity.json`, `report/code/sensitivity.py`; not the primary result)
Same paired 10×5 protocol and corrected intervals, one choice changed at a time (accuracies in %, difference LR − k-NN in pp):

| variant | LR | k-NN | diff | corrected 95% CI | p | folds LR/kNN better | median k |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| primary (seed 20261017) | 95.40 | 94.47 | 0.93 | [−2.51, 4.38] | 0.59 | 16 / 9 | 8 |
| seed 1 | 95.73 | 94.80 | 0.93 | [−3.17, 5.04] | 0.65 | 15 / 11 | 8 |
| seed 2 | 95.73 | 94.93 | 0.80 | [−3.02, 4.62] | 0.68 | 17 / 13 | 8 |
| seed 3 | 95.60 | 95.60 | 0.00 | [−3.59, 3.59] | 1.00 | 12 / 12 | 9 |
| seed 4 | 95.60 | 95.00 | 0.60 | [−2.89, 4.09] | 0.73 | 16 / 10 | 9 |
| seed 5 | 95.40 | 95.53 | −0.13 | [−3.43, 3.16] | 0.94 | 14 / 15 | 8 |
| no standardisation | 96.33 | 95.60 | 0.73 | [−1.92, 3.39] | 0.58 | 13 / 6 | 7 |
| LR with C tuned by inner CV | 95.73 | 94.47 | 1.27 | [−2.38, 4.91] | 0.49 | 17 / 6 | 8 |

Every variant's corrected interval contains 0; the sign of the mean difference flips under one other seed (seed 5). The conclusion "no detectable difference" does not depend on the split seed, the scaling or LR tuning. The split seed moves each method's mean accuracy by up to ~1 point, which is about as large as the observed difference.
